This product includes software developed by Vadym Chernets, as part of Poly A1.

The decision chain follows the notes on decision models collected for Poly A1 (the JEV notes, read
2026-10-02): "exact cache -> similar cache -> deterministic code -> local model -> cheap cloud model ->
if uncertain, a stronger model", and the confidence gate "confidence > .95 -> act; .70-.95 -> verify;
< .70 -> escalate" (92.txt, lines 575-648); "pay for a hosted decision model only after it is shown to
beat cache, rules and a local model" (92.txt, lines 340-360 and 471); structured results through MCP
outputSchema (93.txt, lines 157-159) and retrieval without a vector database (93.txt, line 206).

No third-party code is copied. The adapters speak the published interfaces of these projects, run as
separate programs the company installs itself:
- strands-decider (Apache-2.0): https://github.com/strands-labs/strands-decider - the `ask` command's
  "choice -> option (confidence x)" line and the POST /v1/systemone request and answer shape.
- OpenJev (Apache-2.0): https://github.com/razorback16/openjev - the Jev-compatible /v1/systemone shape.
- JevK5 (Apache-2.0): https://github.com/allebee/jevk5
- Claude Code `claude -p --output-format json --json-schema`: the `structured_output` field.
Every candidate program in data/candidates.json names its page, licence and the day it was read.
